# Land work on main

This project does not use stacked PRs. No Graphite stacks, no `gt submit --stack`, no PR whose base is another feature branch.

Every branch is created from `origin/main`. Every PR targets `main`. GitHub `MERGED` is not enough: the commits must be ancestors of `origin/main` before treating a slice as done or deleting its `*Plan`.

## What this prevents

PR #14 (middleware) used base `feat/implement-execution`. That parent had already merged to `main`. Merging the child into the dead parent stranded the pipe off trunk. `main` still had only `MiddlewarePlan.cs`.

## Opening a PR

```bash
# ❌ BAD — stacked / Graphite / parent feature as base
git switch -c feat/middleware feat/implement-execution
gh pr create --base feat/implement-execution
gt submit --stack

# ✅ GOOD — one slice, branched from trunk, PR to main
git fetch origin
git switch -c feat/implement-middleware origin/main
gh pr create --base main
```

If `gh pr view --json baseRefName` is anything other than `main`, retarget to `main` (rebase onto `origin/main` first) before merge. Do not wait for the user to notice.

## After merge

```bash
git fetch origin
git merge-base --is-ancestor <commit-sha> origin/main
# also confirm the new files exist on origin/main, not only on feat/*
```

If the commit is not an ancestor of `origin/main`, cherry-pick onto a branch from `origin/main` and open a **new** PR to `main`. Do not force-push a dead parent branch.

## Plans

Do not delete a `*Plan` class, or call a slice done in README, until its types are on `origin/main`.
